{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And He caused to grow.</b> His sustenance without toil." "<b>Pleasing to the sight.</b> Rejoicing and expanding the heart, so as to prepare it for receiving the intellectual influx, as it says: וְהָיָה כְּנַגֵּן הַמְנַגֵּן וַתְּהִי עָלָיו יַד ה׳ (II Kings 3:15)." "<b>The tree of knowledge.</b> That which prompts one to give heed to good and evil. And from this sense: וְהָאָדָם יָדַע (Genesis 4:1) — he gave heed to it. And from this the kinsman is called מוֹדָע, as it says: מוֹדַע לְאִישָׁהּ (Ruth 2:1), whose way is to give heed to the needs of his kinsman, as it says: וְאָח לְצָרָה יִוָּלֵד (Proverbs 17:17)." "<b>Good and evil.</b> To choose what is pleasing even though it harms, and to reject what is not pleasing even though it benefits."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:28:43.745780078Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}